// Expressions and collections
// Six koans, one file. Work downwards with ./koans running.
// Replace __; keep the "// koan:" markers. Each koan runs independently.
// Chapter notes: README.md

// koan: 02.01 — Parentheses change the calculation
// Make this expression produce 21. Parentheses group a subexpression before
// multiplication.

new stdout(`rho:io:stdout`) in {
  stdout!((__ + 2) * 3)
}

// koan: 02.02 — Join two strings
// Produce the string firefly. ++ concatenates strings without inserting spaces.

new stdout(`rho:io:stdout`) in {
  stdout!("fire" ++ __)
}

// koan: 02.03 — Count from zero
// Print 20 from this list. nth selects an element by its zero-based index; the first
// element has index 0.

new stdout(`rho:io:stdout`) in {
  stdout!([10, 20, 30].nth(__))
}

// koan: 02.04 — Look up a named value
// Print 7 by looking up the right key. A map stores values under keys; get retrieves the
// value associated with a key.

new stdout(`rho:io:stdout`) in {
  stdout!({"apples": 7, "pears": 4}.get(__))
}

// koan: 02.05 — Adding to an immutable set
// Make the new set have three elements. Sets hold unique values; add returns a new set
// and size counts its members.

new stdout(`rho:io:stdout`) in {
  stdout!(Set(1, 2).add(__).size())
}

// koan: 02.06 — Numeric types must agree
// Make this equality true. The suffix n denotes an arbitrary-precision integer. Both
// operands of + must have the same numeric type.

new stdout(`rho:io:stdout`) in {
  stdout!((100n + __) == 125n)
}
